  "status": "All three candidate RPM builds pass without diagnostics; source fixes and approved debugger configuration qualified. Actual SDK22 canonical/native checks remain pending.",
  "source_base": "b8c93e6f23ef734cd00ae6d5fbd296569d04c773",
  "root_causes": [
    "Generated argument locals are intentionally unused when installed GEOS predates 3.14. Explicit void casts retain public signatures and version exceptions, without changing compiler flags.",
    "The module uses current peer-aware documentation SDK helpers absent from core21. The spec requires the new module-doc-peers capability supplied by core22. Diagnostic images overlay those exact tested helpers; real SDK22 builds remain required.",
    "Unrequested Java generation and unused CMake variables removed; current guides build cleanly.",
    "LLVM optional name index is unsupported by distribution GDB/debugedit; user approved its removal while preserving all other DWARF sections and symbols."
  ],
  "validation": {
    "reported_cases": 201,
    "assertions": 2306,
    "new_regression": "Three feature gates: supported GEOS3.14 operations, unsupported argument boundaries on 3.12/3.13 and object reuse after exceptions. Normal and Valgrind runs use -b --enable-debug.",
    "metadata": "Each RPM check verifies retained QAMD trailer, separate .gnu_debuglink and absence of embedded debug sections. Final artifacts expose 108 AOT functions, source lines and resolved breakpoints on all targets.",
    "memory_scope": "Candidate3 retained the identical affected C++ binary after an initial test syntax failure; the corrected test is the candidate5 test byte for byte. No C++ changes followed. Zero definite, indirect or possible losses and zero memory errors. Reachable distribution-library globals are retained in full logs.",
    "debug_diagnostic": "Fedora reproduces the already approved GCC/Valgrind missing-DW_AT_abstract_origin family. DWARF entries and disassembly identify TLS initialization wrappers around geos_error_msg. Existing approval: evidence/core-close-rpm-qualification-20261002.json; no suppression."
  },
